<!--
  FISH_TYPES_PATCH_BUILD_1 (2026-09-10) — the strip-sweep the spec doc's §4
  flagged as "starting with a measure, not a grep": which of the planet's
  RULED no-fish biomes (_fish_assignment_proposal.md §3, every entry FINAL,
  nothing reopened here) still carry a donor mod's own live `fishTypes` today.

  MEASURED (live XML read directly off disk, not the offline dump — every def
  below is third-party or vanilla-core content the dump does not index, same
  as the sibling ZBiome_Badlands/ZBiome_DesertOasis patches): of the 24
  §3-listed no-fish waters/dry biomes, **16 painted defs carry a live,
  non-empty `fishTypes` today** (donor default, never touched by this repo):

    Alpha Biomes (workshop 1841354677, packageId sarg.alphabiomes):
      AB_FeraliskInfestedJungle (the_webwork), AB_GelatinousSuperorganism
      (the_slime), AB_MycoticJungle (the_rot), AB_OcularForest
      (the_contagion), AB_PropaneLakes (the_propane_lakes), AB_TarPits
      (the_sump), AB_RockyCrags (forsaken_crags, file Biomes_ForsakenCrags.xml)
    GRiNDTerra Biomes (workshop 3537211820, packageId GRimTerra.Biomesmod):
      BiomeGRimond (the_blue_desert)
    More Vanilla Biomes (workshop 1931453053, packageId zylle.MoreVanillaBiomes):
      ZBiome_Grasslands (the_pyrelands)
    Vanilla/Odyssey core (no donor mod, MayRequire Odyssey only):
      Desert, ExtremeDesert (dune_sea + deep_desert), AridShrubland, LavaField
      (the_forge)
    Advanced Biomes (Continued) (workshop 3541022508, packageId
    Mlie.AdvancedBiomes): PoisonForest (poison_forest), Volcano (the_forge)
    Comigo's Greater Swamps (Continued) (workshop 3620545124, packageId
    zal.comigogreaterswamps): COMIGO_GreaterSwamp_Tropical (the_fever_wood) —
    INHERITED, not own: its `fishTypes` lives on the ABSTRACT PARENT
    `COMIGO_GreaterSwamp`, which is why this patch targets the parent, not the
    child — a raw-XML xpath patch runs BEFORE XmlInheritance.Resolve(), so a
    xpath aimed at the child's own node would silently hit zero matches (a
    documented validate_patch.py trap, CLAUDE.md's own warning). The parent's
    only other children, COMIGO_GreaterSwamp_Temperate/_Cold, are not painted
    anywhere on this frozen world (design/Jawa/worldbuilding/biomes/
    _def_bindings_2026-09-09.md's full painted-def table has no entry for
    either), so stripping the parent is safe — nothing else on this world
    inherits from it. validate_patch.py WARNs that this xpath hits 2 nodes in
    one mod folder (the mod ships a second, structurally-identical
    LoadFolders-gated copy under Compat/WMBP/ for World Map Beautification
    Project compatibility, loaded instead of the base copy when that mod is
    active) — both copies carry the same fishTypes block, so stripping both
    is correct, not the "meant one, add a positional predicate" case the
    warning is written for.

  NOT touched here, and why: `AB_MechanoidIntrusion` (the_rust_cathedral) and
  `Wasteland`/`Scarlands` (already `maxFishPopulation 0`, no `fishTypes` tag —
  already the no-fish state this patch is establishing everywhere else); the
  5 `RUT_`-tier own-authored defs (RUT_TheScald/RUT_TwilightSea/RUT_GreySea/
  RUT_PropaneLake/RUT_NightsideIce) already ship `fishTypes` empty,
  documented, at authoring time; `RUT_BlueDesert`/`BiomeCypreJungle`'s
  `RUT_Greentide` sibling defs are not this world's live paint (see
  BiomeFishTypes_Greentide.xml's own note) so nothing to strip there beyond
  what that file already does; `fall_line`/`the_lantern_deeps`/`wreck_fields`
  bind to no painted def at all (§3's own text). `AB_MiasmicMangrove`
  (the_miasma) is explicitly OUT of this sweep — its own ruling (§1 row 4) is
  "fauna channel, not fishTypes", a different category from §3's FINAL
  no-fish list, and reconciling it is a separate call this item does not make.

  Convention: `PatchOperationConditional` + `PatchOperationRemove` on
  `fishTypes` (killing the bucket data entirely, not just emptying it — there
  is no recognizability fix to apply on a biome that should never fish) plus
  a `PatchOperationReplace` zeroing `maxFishPopulation`, matching the
  no-fish state already shipped on this world's `Wasteland`/`Scarlands`/
  `AB_MechanoidIntrusion`. Every block is Conditional-gated on the target
  xpath so a donor's shape change fails safe (0 hits) instead of silently
  matching nothing elsewhere; confirmed applied via validate_patch.py's live
  xpath hit counts, not assumed from 0-errors alone.
-->
<Patch>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationFindMod">
    <mods>
      <li>Alpha Biomes</li>
    </mods>
    <match Class="PatchOperationSequence">
      <success>Always</success>
      <operations>

        <li Class="PatchOperationConditional" MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey">
          <xpath>/Defs/BiomeDef[defName="AB_FeraliskInfestedJungle"]/fishTypes</xpath>
          <match Class="PatchOperationSequence">
            <success>Always</success>
            <operations>
              <li Class="PatchOperationRemove">
                <xpath>/Defs/BiomeDef[defName="AB_FeraliskInfestedJungle"]/fishTypes</xpath>
              </li>
              <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
                <xpath>/Defs/BiomeDef[defName="AB_FeraliskInfestedJungle"]/maxFishPopulation</xpath>
                <value><maxFishPopulation>0</maxFishPopulation></value>
              </li>
            </operations>
          </match>
        </li>

        <li Class="PatchOperationConditional" MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey">
          <xpath>/Defs/BiomeDef[defName="AB_GelatinousSuperorganism"]/fishTypes</xpath>
